Bindings: make keeps a ledger of what each engine gave it. A function registered while an
engine's persistent call runs, through amk.func or an import, is appended once to the
variable <engine>.__fxns__; each name an import returns that is not a function is
appended once to <engine>.__vars__. $(amk.fxns? engines) and $(amk.vars? engines) read
those lists for the named engines, and amk.__fxns__ and amk.__vars__ read them for every
engine in the build. The question mark joins the characters a function name may hold,
as the star did.

